      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Abdominal pain associated with nausea and vomiting in a young patient led to a diagnosis of median arcuate ligament syndrome. The presence of mild haematuria was associated with a concomitant Nutcracker syndrome. Diagnosis was achieved by a computed tomography scan, which showed compression of the vessels of the coeliac axis and left renal vein. These syndromes are very rare, and their association in the same patient has not been described before. There is no relationship in the aetiology of these entities. In this report we discuss the diagnosis and therapeutic options, and review the literature."},
